{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LinIf_00030","versions":[{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LinIf_00030","release":"R19-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LinIf_00030","release":"R20-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LinIf_00030","release":"R21-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LinIf_00030","release":"R22-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LinIf_00030","release":"R23-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LinIf_00030@rel:R24-11#b78d142b","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LinIf_00030","release":"R24-11","content":"[SWS_LinIf_00030] ⌈The LIN Interface shall determine the status of the LIN Driver\nmodule by calling the function Lin_GetStatus earliest after the maximum frame\nlength and latest when the next schedule entry is due.⌋\nIt is up to the LIN Interface module’s implementer to find an efficient way to determine\nthe status check of the LIN Driver. The normal implementation would be that the sta-\ntus is checked within each LinIf_MainFunction_<LinIfChannel.ShortName>\nfunction call after the maximum frame length has passed. In this case, the frame trans-\nmission is still going on (busy). Therefore the status determination shall be checked\nagain within the next LinIf_MainFunction_<LinIfChannel.ShortName> func-\ntion call (if the current LinIf_MainFunction_<LinIfChannel.ShortName> does\nnot start a new frame, of course).\nThe Figure 7.1 shows an example of how the frame transmission is initiated and con-\nfirmed on the bus.\nFigure 7.1: Lin_GetStatus call exampl